<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices fall on rising arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices fall on rising arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean fell on rising arrivals in central Indian markets on Thursday with prices down by 50-100 rupees per tonne on arrivals of around 20,000 tonnes, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in limited trade on steady undertone. Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm. Soymeal yellow was $275-276 per tonne in export while rapeseed extraction was $135-136.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,650 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,600-4,625 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
